## Appendix B: Glossary of Key Terms

| Term | Definition | Source |
|------|-----------|--------|
| **DPVI** | Decompose-Parallelize-Verify-Iterate. Universal workflow pattern independently discovered by 4 organizations | Jones, Mar 11 |
| **Observation Library** | Expanded from Rejection Library. Structured collection of all evaluator observations (rejections and validated successes), each encoding a constraint or promoting a pattern. Three-category taxonomy with saturation-breaking mechanisms. Primary self-improvement engine | Jones, Mar 10; ECC instinct pipeline; "Mind the Gap" ICLR 2025 `[SYNTHESIS UPDATE]` |
| **RESEARCH.md** | Engagement specification file that every agent reads, every output validates against, every deliverable traces to | This capstone, informed by Jones, Mar 27 |
| **Specification Engine** | The Orchestrator reframed: translates vague questions into precise specifications. Quality ceiling of the system | Jones, Jan 21; Feb 10; Mar 24 |
| **Confidence Map** | Structured output of Deliberation: five-tier taxonomy (>80%, 60-80%, 50-60%, <50%, Insufficient Evidence) with DiscoUQ computational features and ACH matrix for contested claims | This capstone; DiscoUQ March 2026; ICD 203 `[SYNTHESIS UPDATE]` |
| **CitationProcessor** | Discrete pipeline stage between L1 (Research) and L1.5 (Deliberation). Deduplicates sources, scores cross-agent corroboration, verifies URL liveness, produces citation manifest | Anthropic Engineering blog; PROV-AGENT W3C `[SYNTHESIS UPDATE]` |
| **Sprint Contract** | Negotiated quality specification between the structuring agent and evaluator defining what "done" looks like for each section | Anthropic, *Harness Design* |
| **Hallucination Tax** | The hidden cost of verifying AI output that has no data grounding. Makes scaffolds (templates without data access) net-negative on productivity | Prendergast, Wealth Management Plugin |
| **Goldman-Grade** | Quality bar: would a domain expert at a top firm call this output "solid on its own merits?" Not "impressive for AI" — actually solid | Jones, Feb 13 |
| **Anti-Slop** | Design principle: every output directly usable without cleanup or reformatting | Jones, Jan 14 |
| **The 201 Gap** | Market gap between AI capability (101) and applied judgment (201). Keystone Intelligence Engine = the 201 layer for consulting | Jones, Jan 25 |
| **The 4:1 Ratio** | Four engineering problems (solved/solvable) to one specification problem (where all value lives) in AI deployment | Jones, Mar 24 |
| **Coordination Tax** | 60–70% of knowledge work hours consumed by coordination overhead, not value creation | Jones, Mar 12 |
| **Expansion Thesis** | When execution cost drops 10x, do 10x more work, not the same work with fewer people | Jones, Mar 14 |
| **Middleware Trap** | Systems built on someone else's intelligence layer are structurally fragile. Moat must be accumulated knowledge | Jones, Mar 19 |
| **Compressed Window** | Platform-building timelines collapsed from decades to months. Waiting = losing | Jones, Feb 14 |
| **Task-vs-Job Boundary** | Agents handle tasks (bounded, specified) well but jobs (contextual stewardship, institutional knowledge) poorly | Jones, Mar 21 |
| **Structure Over Intent** | Outcomes must be determined by architecture, not by hoping agents choose to comply. Structural enforcement > prompt instructions | Jones, Feb 22 |
| **Capability-Dissipation Gap** | Distance between what AI can do and what organizations have reorganized around doing. Where outsized returns live | Jones, Feb 26 |
| **Frontier Operations** | Five operations at the expanding AI capability boundary: boundary sensing, seam design, failure model maintenance, capability forecasting, leverage calibration | Jones, Mar 1 |
| **Harness > Model** | Value accrues to the engineering infrastructure wrapping the model, not to the model itself. The wrapper is the product | Jones, Dec 27; Jan 6; Mar 6 |
| **Intelligence Inversion** | Dumb agents + smart orchestration outperforms smart agents + loose coordination | Jones, Jan 26 |
| **Scarcity Inversion** | When execution gets cheap, clarity, ambition, distribution, and relationships become scarce | Jones, Jan 15 |
| **Correction-Compounding** | Every quality correction permanently modifies the system, creating monotonically improving calibration over time | Jones, Feb 5 |
| **Trajectory Storage** | Full decision log of each completed project — research questions, sources, frameworks, evaluator feedback, quality scores | @Khaliqgant; this capstone |

---

*This plan synthesizes insights from 5 Anthropic engineering articles, 19 high-value X bookmarks, Google's 64-page AI Agents Technical Guide, the everything-claude-code repository (28 agents, 116 skills, 1,421 tests), John Prendergast's Wealth Management Plugin analysis, and the complete systematic analysis of Nate Jones's 91-article Substack corpus (Dec 27, 2025 – Mar 27, 2026; ~1.3M characters of source material analyzed through 18 parallel sub-agents). v3 synthesis updates (marked with `[SYNTHESIS UPDATE]`) incorporate findings from 16 deep research reports across four threads (Open Source Landscape, Quality Standards, Architecture, Frontier), drawing on 80+ peer-reviewed papers including NeurIPS 2025, ICLR 2025/2026, EMNLP 2023/2024, and ACL 2025 publications. Every architectural decision traces to a specific, cited source. The plan was designed to be read at the level of a top-tier capstone at IU Kelley — intellectually rigorous, practically detailed, and honest about what's proven versus experimental.*
